  "question": {
    "text": "The real number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> for which the equation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;has two distinct real roots in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp;belongs to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "lies between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "does not exist.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "lies between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "lies between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>.",
